# The game keeps all its state in the query string, never in paths, so any
# unknown path should still serve the app rather than a 404.
#
# This lives in public/ so Vite copies it INTO dist. netlify.toml only applies
# to a git-connected build — a drag-and-drop of the dist folder never sees it,
# and would silently lose these rules.
# ...EXCEPT AN ASSET, and this rule has to come first because the first match
# wins. Every painted plate in this game degrades through Art's `fallback`, and
# that degradation is driven by the img tag's onError. A catch-all that answers
# 200 with the app shell means a missing .webp is not an error at all: onError
# never fires, the fallback never runs, and the player gets a broken-image glyph
# where a graceful stand-in was designed to be. GitHub Pages 404s these already,
# which is why it has never been seen; a Netlify build would show all of them.
/art/*      /art/:splat        404
/assets/*   /assets/:splat     404

/*  /index.html  200
